IMPLEMENTATION: Route/DTO shape looks fine for a Sprint 1 scaffold, but flagging a modelling gap against the root README's "Deadline and Task Tracker" blurb: the README describes tasks that can have subtasks/checklist items, yet `TaskEntity` has no self-referencing relationship (no `ParentTaskId`/`ParentTask`, no `ChildrenTasks` collection) and `TaskDto`/`CreateTaskRequestDto`/`ModifyTaskRequestDto` have no field to link a task to a parent. As it stands, this schema can only represent a flat list of tasks, not the hierarchy the feature description implies. Recommend adding a nullable self-referencing FK (`ParentTaskId` -> `TaskEntity.Id`) plus a matching EF Core migration before this is built on further, since retrofitting a self-reference after client code exists is more disruptive.

REVIEW: Confirmed - this is a real, evidence-backed gap (grep of `Models/TaskEntity.cs` and the three Task DTOs shows no parent/child field anywhere), not a stylistic nit, and it directly contradicts the subtask/checklist behavior the feature is supposed to support. Recommend treating this as a blocking follow-up before the schema is considered final for Sprint 1.

